    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0137" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d62-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-26">October 26, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret from Harry Hopkins to
                        W. Averell Harriman.</p>
                <p>If meeting in Bosra [<hi rendition="#italic">Basra</hi>] agreed to President
                    confident that between ourselves and the British we can make proper arrangements
                    with Iran and Iraq relative to Russian troops.</p>
                <p>Reports of the Conference are very encouraging although, naturally, everyone here
                    disappointed that personal conference seems difficult.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
